module

public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedCategory.LocallyGivenOfGlobalObject
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.StrictlyPerfect.NonDegenerateGradedDualWitness

/-!
# A covering collection of opens that does not contain the whole space

`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.HasGluingForHomsOver` — the sheaf condition of [Stacks, Tag 0D66] part (2)
in the vocabulary of Situation 0D67, and the hypothesis on which the uniqueness clause of
[Stacks, Tag 0D68] rests — is proved for every covering collection by
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.hasGluingForHomsOver_of_covers`.  Before that it was inhabited only by
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.hasGluingForHomsOver_locallyGivenOfTop`, and that inhabitant is
**degenerate**: every inhabitant obtainable from
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.hasGluingForHomsOver_of_covered_mem` forces `⊤` into the collection, and
when `⊤` is a member `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.exists_unique_solutionIso_of_top_mem` already proves
the conclusion with no granted hypothesis at all.  So the degeneracy criterion for that predicate
is exactly `⊤ ∈ S.opens`, and a carrier meeting the hypotheses while missing `⊤` is what shows
the general statement says more than the degenerate case.

This file names a **concrete carrier** on which that criterion is not met: `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)`,
covered by the two complementary basic opens of its idempotents, both proper.  The collection of
the opens contained in one of the two then covers the space, satisfies hypothesis (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 0D68] on intersections, and does **not** contain `⊤` —
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.exists_covering_collection_top_notMem`.
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.locallyGivenOfGlobal` supplies a system carried by it, for any global
object, and `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.hasGluingForHomsOver_of_covers` applies to that system, so a
non-degenerate inhabitant of the predicate is available.  The same collection, in the form
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.opensLEPair`, carries the non-degeneracy certificate of the comparison
isomorphism of [Stacks, Tag 0D69],
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.exists_locallyGiven_overlapIso_top_notMem`.

The general facts about the collection of opens contained in one of two given opens — that it
covers, that its intersections are unions of members, and that it contains `⊤` only when one of
the two opens is `⊤` — are deliberately **not** redeclared here: they are
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.opensLEPair` and its lemmas in
`StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedCategory.FiniteCoverGlueingNonDegeneracy`.  The
three instances this file needs are discharged inline, so nothing here duplicates a name.

## The degeneracy criterion of Tag 0D6B does *not* apply here

`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.eq_top_of_isGreatest` says that an **increasing** cover `W : E → L`
indexed by a linear order with a greatest element `g` has `W g = ⊤`, so that a datum of
[Stacks, Tag 0D6B] over a finite index set is degenerate and a non-degenerate one needs an
infinite strictly increasing chain of proper opens, hence a non-noetherian carrier.

That criterion is about the datum of Tag 0D6B.  It does **not** transfer to
`HasGluingForHomsOver`, whose collection is an arbitrary *set* of opens carrying neither an index
order nor a monotonicity condition: nothing forces a member to contain every other member, so
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.eq_top_of_isGreatest` has no instance to be applied at.  The collection
below is finite in the only sense that matters — it is generated by two opens — it lives on a
noetherian carrier, and `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.idempotentOpen_fst_ne_top` together with
`..._snd_ne_top` shows it does not contain `⊤`.  So for this predicate a non-degenerate witness
neither needs nor benefits from a non-noetherian space.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.specULiftProdRingedSpace` — the ringed space `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)`, at an
  arbitrary universe, via `ULift`.
* `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.idempotentOpen` — the basic open of an element, as an open of that
  ringed space.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.sup_idempotentOpen_eq_top`,
  `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.idempotentOpen_fst_ne_top` and
  `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.idempotentOpen_snd_ne_top` — `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)` is covered by two proper
  opens.
* `Stacks.DerivedGlueing.exists_covering_collection_top_notMem` — the three conditions bundled,
  at that carrier.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D68](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D68)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D66](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D66)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D6B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D6B)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

namespace Stacks.DerivedGlueing

universe u

/-! ### A concrete carrier: `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)`, covered by two proper opens -/

section Concrete

/-- **The ringed space `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)`**, placed in the universe the ringed-space apparatus of
this tree is stated at, exactly as
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.OnSpace.specULiftIntRingedSpace` places `Spec ℤ`. -/
def specULiftProdRingedSpace : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u} :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec
      (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)))).toLocallyRingedSpace.toRingedSpace

/-- The basic open of an element of `ℤ × ℤ`, as an open of `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)`. -/
def idempotentOpen (a : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) : Opens (specULiftProdRingedSpace.{u}).carrier :=
  PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen a

/-- **`Spec (ℤ × ℤ)` is covered by the basic opens of its two idempotents.**  They span the unit
ideal, since they add up to `1`. -/
theorem sup_idempotentOpen_eq_top :
    idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(1, 0)⟩ ⊔ idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(0, 1)⟩ = ⊤ := by
  have hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun b : Bool =>
      if b then (⟨(1, 0)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) else ⟨(0, 1)⟩) = ⊤ := by
    rw [Ideal.eq_top_iff_one]
    have h : (1 : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) =
        (⟨(1, 0)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) + (⟨(0, 1)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) := by
      apply ULift.ext
      exact Prod.ext (by simp) (by simp)
    rw [h]
    exact Ideal.add_mem _
      (Ideal.subset_span ⟨true, by simp⟩) (Ideal.subset_span ⟨false, by simp⟩)
  have h := (PrimeSpectrum.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top_iff
    (f := fun b : Bool => if b then (⟨(1, 0)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) else ⟨(0, 1)⟩)).mpr hspan
  rw [iSup_bool_eq] at h
  exact h

/-- The two idempotents multiply to zero, so their basic opens are disjoint. -/
theorem inf_idempotentOpen_eq_bot :
    idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(1, 0)⟩ ⊓ idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(0, 1)⟩ = ⊥ := by
  have hzero : (⟨(1, 0)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) * (⟨(0, 1)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) = 0 := by
    apply ULift.ext
    exact Prod.ext (by simp) (by simp)
  exact (((PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen_mul (⟨(1, 0)⟩ : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)) ⟨(0, 1)⟩).symm.trans
      (congrArg PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen hzero)).trans
    ((PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen_eq_bot_iff (0 : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ))).mpr IsNilpotent.zero))

/-- The basic open of a nonzero idempotent is not empty: the idempotent is not nilpotent. -/
private theorem idempotentOpen_ne_bot_of_isIdempotentElem {a : ULift.{u} (ℤ × ℤ)}
    (ha : IsIdempotentElem a) (h0 : a ≠ 0) : idempotentOpen.{u} a ≠ ⊥ := fun h =>
  h0 (ha.eq_zero_of_isNilpotent ((PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen_eq_bot_iff a).mp h))

/-- The basic open of the second idempotent is not empty: the idempotent is not nilpotent. -/
theorem idempotentOpen_snd_ne_bot : idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(0, 1)⟩ ≠ ⊥ :=
  idempotentOpen_ne_bot_of_isIdempotentElem (by simp [IsIdempotentElem, ULift.ext_iff])
    (by simp [ULift.ext_iff])

/-- The basic open of the first idempotent is not empty. -/
theorem idempotentOpen_fst_ne_bot : idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(1, 0)⟩ ≠ ⊥ :=
  idempotentOpen_ne_bot_of_isIdempotentElem (by simp [IsIdempotentElem, ULift.ext_iff])
    (by simp [ULift.ext_iff])

/-- **The first of the two opens is proper.**  If it were everything, its intersection with the
second would be the second, and that intersection is empty while the second is not. -/
theorem idempotentOpen_fst_ne_top : idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(1, 0)⟩ ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro h
  refine idempotentOpen_snd_ne_bot.{u} ?_
  rw [← inf_idempotentOpen_eq_bot, h, top_inf_eq]

/-- **The second of the two opens is proper.** -/
theorem idempotentOpen_snd_ne_top : idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(0, 1)⟩ ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro h
  refine idempotentOpen_fst_ne_bot.{u} ?_
  rw [← inf_idempotentOpen_eq_bot, h, inf_top_eq]

/-- **A covering collection on a concrete noetherian carrier that does not contain `⊤`.**  The
collection of opens of `Spec (ℤ × ℤ)` contained in one of the two basic opens of its idempotents
covers the space, satisfies hypothesis (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0D68] on intersections, and does not
contain `⊤`.

This is the collection a non-degenerate inhabitant of
`Stacks.DerivedGlueing.HasGluingForHomsOver` is to be carried by, and it is what shows that no
non-noetherian carrier is needed for that predicate — see the section *The degeneracy criterion
of Tag 0D6B does not apply here* of the module documentation. -/
theorem exists_covering_collection_top_notMem :
    ∃ ℬ : Set (Opens (specULiftProdRingedSpace.{u}).carrier),
      sSup ℬ = ⊤ ∧
      (∀ A ∈ ℬ, ∀ B ∈ ℬ, A ⊓ B = sSup {W | W ∈ ℬ ∧ W ≤ A ⊓ B}) ∧
      (⊤ : Opens (specULiftProdRingedSpace.{u}).carrier) ∉ ℬ := by
  classical
  set U := idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(1, 0)⟩ with hU
  set V := idempotentOpen.{u} ⟨(0, 1)⟩ with hV
  refine ⟨{W | W ≤ U ∨ W ≤ V}, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact le_antisymm le_top
      (le_of_eq_of_le sup_idempotentOpen_eq_top.symm
        (sup_le (le_sSup (Or.inl le_rfl)) (le_sSup (Or.inr le_rfl))))
  · intro A hA B _
    exact le_antisymm
      (le_sSup ⟨hA.imp inf_le_left.trans inf_le_left.trans, le_rfl⟩)
      (sSup_le fun _ hW => hW.2)
  · exact fun h =>
      h.elim (fun hle => idempotentOpen_fst_ne_top (top_le_iff.mp hle))
        fun hle => idempotentOpen_snd_ne_top (top_le_iff.mp hle)

end Concrete

end Stacks.DerivedGlueing

end
